":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"SSH key + sudo from your workstation (operator client)"},"753":{"id":"/getting-started-25","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"**Out-of-band console** (IPMI/iDRAC) — heavy Jobs can still wedge SSH if you skip Guard"},"754":{"id":"/getting-started-26","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Operator client (the machine that runs Ansible and `manage.sh`): Ansible ≥ 2.14, kubectl, helm, **bazelisk**"},"755":{"id":"/getting-started-27","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"One command installs and verifies everything (Homebrew, no sudo):"},"756":{"id":"/getting-started-28","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Same script, apt/dnf based:"},"757":{"id":"/getting-started-29","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Install WSL2 + Ubuntu once (PowerShell), then the same script inside WSL:"},"758":{"id":"/getting-started-30","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"`status` subcommand reports what is already present; see Shell reference for the full contract."},"759":{"id":"/getting-started-31","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Never proceed without inventory ping and OOB access. Do not start kimi / Mode B/C until `start-test` succeeds."},"760":{"id":"/getting-started-32","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"The declarative topology `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml` is the single source of truth for\n**all five configurations** — node names/IPs, fabric, switch port map, and which Spark is\nthe orchestrator. Edit it, then render:"},"761":{"id":"/getting-started-33","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Rendering produces the Ansible inventory (`ansible/inventory/hosts.ini`, gitignored),\nfabric group vars, per-node netplan, and per-node cloud-init user-data — all from the\ntopology file. Full model: Lab topology."},"762":{"id":"/getting-started-34","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: none`, one node with `role: orchestrator`. No high-speed cabling, local NCCL only."},"763":{"id":"/getting-started-35","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: pair`, two nodes with `hs_ifs` (one 200 Gb/s QSFP cable). `group_vars` `highspeed_*`\nis the **pair** NCCL reference."},"764":{"id":"/getting-started-36","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: ring`, three nodes, QSFP triangle. **Not** “2-node plus spark2 with pair env” —\ncabling and Job env: LiteLLM rounded stack."},"765":{"id":"/getting-started-37","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: switch` + `switch:` block (CRS804-4DDQ-hRM `port_map`, one entry per node; 5 nodes\nuse breakout lanes `sfpplus4a`/`sfpplus4b`). Do **not** paste 2-node `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME`\nonto switch hops without reading Interconnect & NCCL."},"766":{"id":"/getting-started-38","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Any node may be the orchestrator — see Choose topology → Pick your orchestrator."},"767":{"id":"/getting-started-39","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Verify:"},"768":{"id":"/getting-started-40","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Expected: pong on every host. If not: SSH keys, management firewall, console `ip a`."},"769":{"id":"/getting-started-41","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Still prefer a manual `hosts.ini`? `cp ansible/inventory/hosts.ini.example ansible/inventory/hosts.ini`\nand edit it — the classic path still works, it just skips the generated netplan / cloud-init."},"770":{"id":"/getting-started-42","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"Render early OS / highspeed user-data **before** or as the first part of bootstrap."},"771":{"id":"/getting-started-43","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"With a `lab.yaml` in place, user-data is generated per node at\n`ansible/files/generated/cloud-init/user-data-<node>.yaml` (all five fabrics). The static\nexamples `ansible/cloud-init/example-user-data-1node.yaml` / `example-user-data-2node.yaml`\nremain for ad-hoc labs. Feed rendered YAML via vendor BMC, or apply manually and reboot."},"772":{"id":"/getting-started-44","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"Extra-var `apply_now=true` writes user-data on the node and can reboot it. Inference must already be stopped. Default is render-only."},"773":{"id":"/getting-started-45","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"To import prep from bootstrap: `--extra-vars run_cloud_init_prep=true`."},"774":{"id":"/getting-started-46","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"The playbook installs prereqs, highspeed netplan on 2+ nodes (from the generated per-node\nnetplan when present), K3s server on the **orchestrator** node (`role: orchestrator` in\n`lab.yaml`), agents, labels, kubeconfig."},"775":{"id":"/getting-started-47","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"Verify:"},"776":{"id":"/getting-started-48","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"Expected (2-node example):"},"777":{"id":"/getting-started-49","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getti